oper would normally go  to discover and interact with rest apis  in order to understand how they work  in graphql the portal actually is a  built-in playground that accommodates  development it's almost like a built-in  ide  and so it allows you to explore new  queries on the fly and use things like  tab completion in order to discover  those queries in order to  learn how to use them better and so  we're not here to talk about whether you  should use graphql or rest  our philosophy is that you should use  graphql and rest  and i think one of the best ways to do  that is to take some of our rest-based  practices and apply them to graphql  this is something that we've seen in the  market this is something that we really  see working really well in a number of  customers and so we wanted to bring  those to you  so that you could leverage them and  understand what those are  the basis of this philosophy is that  apis are digital products  apis are a way for an enterprise to take  its assets and put it in the hands of  developers  whether those developers are internal  employees partners  or external customers in order to grow  the company's leverage of those assets  because apis are digital products we  rely on developers having a consistent  experience  in order to understand how to use those  digital products and build the  compelling experiences  they need in order to bring your assets  to market  and so consistency is incredibly  important because developer friction  is a is a huge challenge in  adoption of apis and in growth  strategies of digital companies  consistency in graphql really starts  with well-formed graphql and i think we  can learn a lot about that from  well-formed rest  you would never expect a well-formed  rest query to be list employees by  department  that sounds like a java function a  well-conformed rest query would be  a resource right get employees and you  pass employees id  and so that is what we consider wealth  and rest right nouns and t